WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.517 --> 00:00:02.700
ROGER MARTINEZ: Hi, Roger
here from Google Cloud.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.290
And in this video,
we'll have a look

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.230
at how Contact Center AI can
help the financial services

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.110
industry by transforming
your customer service.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.170
Various external events,
like natural disasters,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.900
can have serious impacts
on financial institutions.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.090
Such events can create
an influx of requests

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.580
from customers looking for
information and support.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.150
But limited human resources,
unprecedented network

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.100
infrastructure loads,
and restrictions

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.660
on travel and
working from offices

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.240
can hinder financial services
organization's ability

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.640
to deliver critical
services to their customers

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:33.930
and communities.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.510
This can put a huge strain
on a number of infrastructure

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.340
and core business systems.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.200
One area that bears
the most strain

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.880
is where customers
directly interface

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.730
of your business, things like
call centers and customer

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.655
support lines can see
unprecedented volume increases.

00:00:47.655 --> 00:00:49.530
And if you're not set
up to handle the scale,

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.930
your customers could suffer.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.710
For example long wait times
on hold or an email query

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.900
going too long before
being responded to,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.600
can lead to unhappy
customers, and potentially

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.670
long live conversations
that drive up

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.410
costs for call centers.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.020
The simplest solution is to
increase your service forces

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.740
to respond to demand.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:11.700
But that's not always
as easy as it sounds.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.190
The costs of hiring and
training new support workers

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:17.790
can have a significant impact
on your operational efficiency

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.680
and your profitability.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.890
The bottom line is, that during
times of high volume customer

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.050
needs, your company
will have to find

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.210
the balance between offering
exceptional customer

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:30.930
service and personalized
intuitive customer care,

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.720
while increasing
operational efficiency.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.560
Thankfully, Google Cloud
Contact Center AI, CCAI,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.030
is here to help.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.290
CCAI uses artificial
intelligence

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.260
to converse naturally
with customers,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.100
and expertly assess human
agents on more complex cases.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.120
CCAI's conversational core
powers three key features.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.970
Virtual Agent gives
customers 24/7 access

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.010
to immediate
conversational self-service

00:01:56.010 --> 00:02:00.230
with seamless hand-offs to human
agents for more complex issues.

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.370
Agent Assist
empowers human agents

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.140
with continued support
during their calls

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.120
by identifying intent
and providing real time,

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.910
step by step assistance.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.340
Insights uses natural
language processing

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.590
to identify call drivers
and sentiment that helps.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:17.190
Contact Center managers learn
about customer interactions

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.360
to improve call outcomes.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.180
Let's see how
Contact Center AI is

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.385
helping transform the
financial services industry.

00:02:23.385 --> 00:02:24.966
[RINGTONE]

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.160
VIRTUAL AGENT: Hi, Prisha,
thanks for calling our bank.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.810
How can I help?

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.545
PRISHA: Hi, I'd
like to pay my bill.

00:02:32.545 --> 00:02:33.420
VIRTUAL AGENT: Great.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.940
Can you please
verify your address?

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.350
PRISHA: 15 State Street.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.127
Oh, and how much is it?

00:02:39.127 --> 00:02:40.710
ROGER MARTINEZ:
Virtual Agent provides

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.990
immediate conversational
support, with customers

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.820
directing the flow.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.590
VIRTUAL AGENT: You owe $150.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:49.710
Do you want to pay with
the account ending in 1337?

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.037
PRISHA: Yes, please.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:51.870
VIRTUAL AGENT: Done.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.460
I've sent an email confirmation.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.810
Is there anything else?

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.185
ROGER MARTINEZ:
Virtual agent can

00:02:56.185 --> 00:02:58.590
take care of basic
fulfillment on the spot.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:02.165
PRISHA: Yes, actually, there's
a $35 charge I don't recognize.

00:03:02.165 --> 00:03:03.540
VIRTUAL AGENT:
From last week, it

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.580
looks like it's
an overdraft fee.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.980
PRISHA: Oh, that's not fair.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.037
I didn't know.

00:03:09.037 --> 00:03:10.620
VIRTUAL AGENT: OK,
let me transfer you

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.118
to a specialist to help.

00:03:12.118 --> 00:03:14.160
ROGER MARTINEZ: More
complex cases are seamlessly

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.630
handed off to a human agent.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.378
[RINGTONE]

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.070
ELLIOTT: Hi,
Prisha, I'm Elliott.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.950
I see you're concerned
about the overdraft fee.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.898
PRISHA: Yeah, I didn't
know I would get charged.

00:03:25.898 --> 00:03:27.690
ELLIOTT: OK, I can
waive the fee this time,

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.400
but would you like
overdraft protection,

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.213
so it doesn't happen again?

00:03:31.213 --> 00:03:32.880
ROGER MARTINEZ: Agent
Assist listens in,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.580
giving real time,
step by step guidance.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.350
PRISHA: Yes, please.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.670
ELLIOTT: OK, I've set it up.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.260
Is there anything else?

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.150
PRISHA: No, this was great.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.770
Thanks a lot.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.500
ROGER MARTINEZ: Lastly, Insights
gives you real time visibility

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:49.535
into key called
drivers and sentiment.

00:03:49.535 --> 00:03:50.910
But there are so
many more places

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.310
CCAI can be leveraged
in financial services.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.597
For example, it can
streamline the user's ability

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:58.680
to manage their account
information, like password

00:03:58.680 --> 00:03:59.640
resets.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.610
Or it can help facilitate
the user paying their bills,

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:04.920
activating or
deactivating credit cards,

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.980
or other types of transactions.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.332
CCAI can help with
bigger scope tasks,

00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:11.790
like helping customers generate
and understand their credit

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.600
scores, and view or redeem
rewards for their memberships

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.000
based upon transactions.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.820
With lots of features
like sentiment analysis,

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.630
multilingual support, automatic
topic determination, and chat

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.900
level analytics, CCAI
provides a versatile tool

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.420
to handle a number of solutions
to improve your customer's

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:32.800
experience with your company.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.740
If you'd like to know
more, visit the link

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.310
in the description below.

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.130
You can also subscribe
to our Cloud YouTube

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.430
channel for more great
Contact Center AI content.

